--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SURFACE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
VehicleSelect is the web canonical per-page vehicle scope picker (web/src/components/forms/
VehicleSelect.tsx). The web component is a controlled <Select> wired to the global useSelectedVehicle()
store: it maps each fleet vehicle to an option whose value is String(v.id) and whose label is
`v.display_name || v.vin || \`Vehicle ${v.id}\``, reflects the current scope via
value={vehicleId != null ? String(vehicleId) : ''}, writes the chosen id back with
setVehicleId(Number.isFinite(next) && next > 0 ? next : null), renders nothing when the fleet is empty,
and can be prefixed with a small decorative <Car/> icon (withIcon). The only key it passes to t() is
t('vehicleSelect.aria', 'Select vehicle').

Data sources (web): useSelectedVehicle (the fleet + scope store) and useTranslation (the i18n facade).
The web store is a plain scope value with NO query-freshness or connectivity dimension, so the web
source has NO stale / offline chrome — fabricating it would be parity drift (the Combobox / DateRangeFilter
presentational-surface precedent). A native scope picker, however, binds the fleet load directly, so it
renders the shared VehicleSelectState holder's loading / empty / error / loaded transitions inline (the
states the web component delegates to its page). The branches reproduced and verified headlessly:
  - loading  — busy chrome (TsSpinner) while the fleet is in flight (and the Idle pre-load state)
  - empty    — friendly empty surface (TsEmptyState), never a blank box (web returns nothing here)
  - error    — TsErrorDisplay with a retry affordance wired to VehicleSelectState.Retry()
  - ready    — the populated ComboBox (the Fluent equivalent of the web <Select>), with the label
               fallback rule, value round-trip, positive-finite commit guard and clamp-to-known-id
  - withIcon — optional leading decorative Segoe Fluent "Car" glyph (\uE804), hidden from Narrator
               (AccessibilityView.Raw) exactly as the web aria-hidden icon
No stale / offline chrome is invented (documented above).

Native decomposition (the shipped 4-file shared-surface pattern; the 3 Microsoft.UI-free files are
compile-linked into TeslaSync.App.Tests and unit-tested headlessly, the WinUI view is exercised by the
app build):
  - VehicleSelect.Model.cs      VehicleSelectRegistration (Slug "VehicleSelect"; translation.vehicleSelect.*
                                keys + English fallbacks — aria is web-verbatim, the rest caption the native
                                loading/empty/error/prompt chrome); VehicleSelectStatus enum; PII-safe
                                VehicleSelectDiagnostics (view.opened slug=VehicleSelect, no fleet/label/id).
  - VehicleSelect.Source.cs     VehicleSelectItem (web {value,label} + id); VehicleSelectProjection — the
                                cached → projection adapter (ToItems reuses the shared VehicleLabels.Short
                                rule = web display_name||vin||`Vehicle ${id}`; ParseValue applies the web
                                Number.isFinite && >0 commit guard).
  - VehicleSelect.ViewModel.cs  VehicleSelectViewModel — the UI-thread-free state holder over the shared
                                P1/S8 VehicleSelectState (web useSelectedVehicle) + ILocalizer (P1/S10):
                                Items, SelectedId/SelectedValue, Status, every resolved caption + AriaLabel
                                (override-or-key), SelectByValue (commit + clamp), Retry, WithIcon.
  - VehicleSelect.cs            The WinUI view: a ComboBox + the shared TsSpinner/TsErrorDisplay/TsEmptyState
                                surfaces + the optional decorative Car FontIcon; binds the view-model,
                                carries the trigger accessible name, and emits view.opened once on Loaded.

Bindings: the view performs NO I/O. It binds the shared P1/S8 state holder
(TeslaSync.App.Core.Forms.VehicleSelectState) and the P1/S10 i18n facade
(TeslaSync.App.Core.Notifications.ILocalizer); the view-model + projection are pure and headless.

