UI-AUTOMATION EXCLUSION EVIDENCE
    The only red on this runner is the out-of-process WinAppDriver/Appium harness (TeslaSync.App.UITests,
    every class [Trait("Category","UIAutomation")] + [Collection(WinAppDriverCollection)]). It is a HARD
    failure by design when no driver/app is present (UiAutomationUnavailableException — "deliberately a
    hard failure, not an xUnit skip"), so the full-solution `dotnet test` with no filter is red SOLELY
    because no WinAppDriver endpoint / WinAppDriver.exe / deployed MSIX exists on this headless runner.
    That E2E runtime is not the WinUI 3 / .NET 10 capability this prompt requires; it is deferred to a
    provisioned UI runner, exactly as every shipped sibling surface recorded.

